VU1 decoded-pair cache decodes on demand. refreshDecodedCodeCache (formerly rebuildDecodedCodeCache) decoded all 2048
pairs of the micro image whenever the VU1 code generation changed, on the VIF1/VU1 worker, and compiledProgramFor
refreshes it on every new generation; most pairs of an image are never executed. The refresh now records the image
identity, clears a per-pair valid bit and derives m_statusUnread / m_statusQuiet from the raw words (the lower opcode
and the upper I bit, the same two values decodeInstructionPair takes); getDecodedInstructionPairForPc decodes a pair
the first time it is asked for. decodeInstructionPair is const and reads no interpreter state, so a pair decodes to
the same value whenever it is decoded: results are bit-identical. compiledProgramFor keeps refreshing because the
compiled program reads m_statusQuiet. Only getDecodedInstructionPairForPc reads the cache.
From huanghuangdaquan-beep/gow-native-pc-optimization (its patch 44), rebased on patches 30-44 here. Measured there
on an i3-4170 (tools/test/vu1_change_cost.cpp): one refresh 39-112 us -> about 1 us. Not yet measured on this
project's hardware (replay bench and A/B FPS pairs pending).

